00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:29.310
<i>Despite the outbreak of a minor Militia rebellion, the incident never grew into an all out coup d'etat.</i>

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.280
<i>Even so, to put an end to the rebellion...</i>

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.320
<i>I had to put my own life at risk and head into battle.</i>

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.200
<i>However, since the incident didn't end up causing anyone harm...</i>

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.750
<i>...I have decided to keep my personal mission a secret.</i>

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.840
<b>Gateway To The Moon</b>

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.190
So, this got jammed here in the attack made by Harry's Gold Type SUMO...

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.400
Did you get it yet, sis?

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.570
What are you...!

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.860
Captain! Lock down the wire!

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:20.870
I know that!

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.960
What's this sound I'm hearing?

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.670
You're sending your people to rendezvous with us?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.760
It must be a direct-line communication.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.680
Are you saying you intend to assassinate Queen Dianna?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.890
Assassinate Queen Dianna!?

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.260
Does this mean even Midgard has plans for something like that?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.770
Such things must not be muttered so carelessly.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.190
That may simply be one option that's open to us.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:54.360
You might say that we of the Ghingnham lineage are tasked with bringing dishonor to the Soriel family.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.280
Such is the ultimate destiny of my family, as soldiers of the Moonrace for generation upon generation.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.280
My fleet will arrive at the rendezvous point shortly. Do not be late.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.370
That won't be a problem. However, the Militia's ship is also trailing closely behind us.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.170
Once the Queen is in my custody...

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.290
You will act as a decoy and lure the enemy.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.460
As a decoy?

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.460
It's a feint on our part.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.260
Your ship will not be destroyed.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.470
Is there no way for me to defy a noble's orders?

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.060
I suppose a military officer acting as a spy can't hope for such.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.980
Muron, there's trouble! We have a problem here!

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:38.280
Just hold on a moment, sis.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.360
That bastard Midgard has betrayed us. He can't be trusted!

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.660
What are you talking about?

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.280
He's about to sell out Queen Dianna!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.290
Sold her out? Why!?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.880
Your majesty, please flee this place and escape with us!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.670
What has happened?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:06.600
Majesty, I don't have time to explain now, but you're currently in grave danger.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.770
...and the channel has been opened.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:16.770
Thank you.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.480
Not at all. Thanks for sharing the frequencies with us.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.280
You sure you're okay with this?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.360
Mr. "Red Glasses" might have plans of his own, you know.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.870
That's true. He's known to be quite the independent thinker.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:37.290
Sir Guin, do you believe that Queen Dianna was kidnapped, like Harry said?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.880
The more a dog loves his master, the more likely he is to bite a threatening man's hand.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.590
In that case, allow me to act as a spy for you again!

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.390
I give up.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:50.680
Only you, Lady Lily, could view outer space as her own personal garden.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:55.390
But, when you contemplate being out here in a place so vast and infinite, how can it not make you excited?

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:59.270
If you ask me, those who get sick out here in space must be crazy!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.570
Is that up or down? Decide!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.570
Lieutenant, isn't there some way for us to reduce these feelings of dizziness!?

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.990
Will you let that beat you when the enemy shows his face?

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.160
Use your willpower and deal with it!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.790
Just remember that we're also closing in on the enemy base. Don't be so weak-willed!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:20.170
Loran said that once we arrive on the moon, there will be <i>some</i> gravity.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.960
You're handling this nicely, Miner.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.170
I'm pretty sure I could get used to this lifestyle!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.680
I'm jealous.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.390
You build planes, floating in the sky should be your specialty!

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.890
Flying is a vastly different thing from floating!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.890
Crikey...

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.980
To feel wind blowing in my face again...

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.060
...The wind would feel wonderful!

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.790
Places without air or gravity are a pain!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.660
Is the Red Team running away?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.460
There it is.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.380
I've had enough of space!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.460
I'll get you to return me to Earth!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:03.880
Here they come...

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.090
Catch!

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.980
Firing inside a spaceship is an idiotic thing to do!

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.070
Muron, I have the shuttle now.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.280
- The shuttle!
- The Shuttle?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.570
They've taken the shuttle!

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.570
You mean the escape shuttle?

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.880
I knew it. They're moonrace, yet they're being weighed down by Earth's gravity!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.290
Being in space must've frightened them.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.090
Ready our mobile suits for pursuit.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.390
There's no need to chase them.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:57.980
If that's the way they are in space, let them turn into mummified corpses and rot.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.060
- Commander Midgard!
- What is it?

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.980
Ghingnham's ship has arrived at the rendezvous on schedule. They're asking us to hurry!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.570
It's time for me to make sure Queen Dianna's ready.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:16.490
You there, men! You as well! We're going to do the exercise once more!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.790
If the Willgem proceeds any further, we'll be too close to the moon.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.880
So we have to dispose of them here.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.170
I never guessed it'd be this much trouble to dispose of two bombs.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.880
But since it's a nuclear bomb...

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.470
I'd ideally like to detonate it somewhere where it won't cause anyone trouble.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.890
Seems like anything that comes from the Dark History always has trouble attached to it.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:38.890
Then what excuse do we use to get permission for the White Doll to head outside?

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.690
You're from the Moonrace, so you think of something!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:45.270
Milady, how long did you know about that?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:48.860
After seeing everything you've done in space, It's obvious.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:55.280
I've always known that something was odd ever since I saw your first meeting with Keith in front of that Museum.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:56.660
Is that so?

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.580
So, then this expedition...

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.500
...is just a trip back home for you?

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.880
I guess so. But, what I'd personally like to do is write a book...

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.790
...about the journey you're all taking to reach the moon.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.420
I really don't know what'll happen to us in the end.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.550
But I'd love to see you publish that title back on earth if we make it.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.220
I agree. Please do!

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.600
I'd like that a lot...

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.640
But since I'm also on this battleship, no-one knows if I'll even survive long enough to get that chance.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.310
How many times must we go over this before you get it!?

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.980
They've both changed quite a bit.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.730
Captain Loran, This is no time to be lounging about!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.740
I'm the Captain of the Gallop!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.650
That's right!

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.070
Now isn't the time for this!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.740
What is it?

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.030
We've intercepted a transmission from Queen Dianna.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.870
A transmission from Dianna? How did we get that?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.960
Please come up to the bridge.
- Okay!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.160
Your Majesty!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.370
Please, it was all circumstantial, so forgive our rudeness!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:31.170
If I had continued to let Midgard mislead me, I... I wouldn't be able to complete my objectives.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.460
I'm grateful for this!

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.760
No way... we're unworthy of such praise!

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.260
Hey sis!

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.350
Queen Dianna has given us a fantastic idea!

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:46.060
There's an artificial satellite called "Mistletoe" nearby.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.770
I'd like you to take me there.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.940
"Mistletoe", you say?

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:55.280
<i>(Translator's note: Muron literally referred to the "Yadorigi" which is the Japanese name for "Mistletoe")</i>

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.650
Like the plant, yadorigi?

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:55.860
It's a small asteroid colony once used for agricultural experimentation in a past age.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.360
You mean such a place actually exists?

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:00.530
Naturally. And also...

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:01.740
Yes?

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.870
This music, please transmit it to the Militia's ship for me.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.460
Y-Yes!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.850
It's a classical sounding melody.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.260
Is that so?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.430
Is my decoding solution not working?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.770
No, it's fine. Let's play it back.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.150
Right. Please do.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.440
Wow, amazing!

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:33.730
What sort of map is this?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.940
It's a chart depicting the space between the earth and moon.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:38.570
That spot is closer to the moon.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.240
- This thing is a map?
- That's right.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:44.530
Alright... So, judging from this chart...

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.040
We should be looking for AC number D-02-3.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.170
It's Mistletoe!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.830
That's kinda weird.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.670
What is it?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.460
It's an abandoned Asteroid Colony.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.760
It's on the edge of the safe-zone where I can dispose of these nuclear bombs.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.060
Queen Dianna must be hiding in that colony.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.640
How can you be sure of that?

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.650
Currently, there isn't anybody living in that Colony, nor is there anybody who'd be monitoring it.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.440
So we need to go to this "Mistletoe" place, Lieutenant?

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.860
Correct.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:18.360
Dianna's garden, "Mistletoe", is it?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.630
Oh, Soul of the moon...!

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:48.770
Reside within! Reside within! Reside within! Our Home... Reside within!

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:57.360
Reside within! Reside within! Reside within!

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.650
The true Queen of the moon!

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:04.240
We're going back to the moon with the Queen!

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.060
It's gonna be tough...

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.490
If we have enough energy, we can open the hatch.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:40.150
Cancer, if you check the upper left corner, there should be a Mobile Suit "key lock".

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.610
I've found it, but it won't move.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.280
Stay right there.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:50.290
I'll try to activate the dock from out here.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.290
Excellent! It seems like it's working!

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.790
Wow! Our Queen's like a magician!

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.380
That's the port's airlock, right?

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.090
I'm going to close off the hatch.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:16.850
Long ago, when the majority of the Moonrace was still in suspended animation...

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.270
The Soriel Family experimented with agricultural to expand our air and food supplies.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.070
Can I open the inner hatch?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.570
Yes. There should be enough air.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.860
Right.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.870
This... is a forest, isn't it!?

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.460
Wow! This is incredible!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:43.380
The two of you should take this shuttle and use it to return to the earth, where there are real forests and oceans.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.170
What are you trying to say, Your Majesty?

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.180
If we were to do that, everything we've done thus far would be for nothing!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:56.350
If it wasn't for you, I would never have made it here, but if you reach the moon now, it could prove dangerous.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:00.060
You can't be sure the Militia will even receive to the message you sent them!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:04.780
My hopes are that your children will someday blend in with the terrans.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:07.650
Please see that it happens, Cancer, Muron.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:11.950
Please don't say something so cruel, Your Majesty!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:29.550
You let Dianna escape after the trouble we went though to bring her here. Is that what you're saying?

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:34.970
Correct. We were pursued by Terrans wielding technology from the Dark History...

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.980
...And after that, we were also betrayed by Lieutenant Harry.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.350
Oh my...

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.060
Lord Gym Ghingnham!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.150
Well, I suppose that girl is the Moon's Queen after all.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:51.660
Given that, I shouldn't be surprised by her fooling someone of such low birth.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:55.580
Are you suggesting that Queen Dianna may have already returned to the moon?

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.470
What is this music?

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.680
It's the song the Soriel family once used for encrypting transmissions.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.390
Queen Dianna is hiding in an abandoned colony.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:16.680
What?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.270
First Team, form an attack position.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.270
Second team, form a defense position.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.860
We're setting off for the asteroid colony, Mistletoe!
- Sir!

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:28.650
Allow me to show you the difference between a 2500 year old noble military family...

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.780
...and some worthless civilian recruited militia!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.080
Hold your position. Stay where you are for now, Merrybell.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.680
Wh... What in the world are you doing, Mahiroo squad!?

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.060
For someone of such low birth...

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.940
...you should be honored to be in the presence of our Mahiroo!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.230
That voice must have been Sweatson Sutero.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.410
He's little more than a blemish who rides on his family's name...

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.090
With your abilities...

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:33.880
That shuttle should be able to handle reentry into the earth's atmosphere. Therefore...

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.680
The sole reason for our living on earth was to help and serve our Queen!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.190
If you understand that, then you cannot turn us away!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.150
Sir Muron, Lady Cancer...

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:54.490
Please, you don't need to mention our titles!

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:59.450
If you're destined to die here, then we're ready to share your fate by your side.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.790
Thank you...

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.880
I expected the Lieutenant wanted to get her back on his own...

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.680
This mission is about saving the Queen of our enemy.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.890
In that case, it should've been left to that "Red Glasses" guy.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:22.680
Sir Guin believes if we left that task to Lieutenant Harry alone...

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.270
...it could undermine our position in the upcoming negotiations.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:29.360
Do you think Sochie can handle it?

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:33.860
Back at the Zacktraeger, Loran gave Sochie a bit of training.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.360
Is the moon truly under the control of Agrippa Maintainer?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:41.660
This is why we will require your power...

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.290
...Lady Kihel Heim.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.580
If I were to pose as Dianna, would that truly help?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:47.580
Yes.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.590
I see. In that case, I will become another Dianna.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:56.470
Lieutenant Harry has plans of his own.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.980
Hey Loran, can't we dispose of the nuclear bombs here? There's nothing around.

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:11.480
That won't do. It's too near the ship's course.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.280
Let's focus on saving Queen Dianna first.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.490
I see it!

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.780
This is it! Mistletoe!

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.290
Queen Dianna's star.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.370
What sort of star is this supposed to be?

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.880
Aren't stars supposed to shine and twinkle?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.750
Oh, this is definitely one of the stars.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.970
This block has completely died off.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.760
The Nano Machines must have died.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:46.980
I've found it, Queen Dianna!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.650
See that? It's there... Center Control.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:56.990
Right, Right! Then, let's head there!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.490
You really want us to go there?

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.780
I would like to activate the equipment here.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:05.080
So that way, we'd have soil, sunlight, and water!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.880
After Dianna's authority is restored...

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:20.380
I will return to being what I was before... The daughter of a mine owner, running a mine in the mountains.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.760
Yes.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.180
I can be happy in that life...

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.850
...but it will also feel rather lonely.
- You mean Empty?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:30.690
That's not it. I'm really not like Dianna...

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.850
After you.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:40.570
I've discovered Dianna never runs from her responsibility, no matter what pressure or stress she may be under.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:43.450
That is why she's so beautiful.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:47.870
Your ability to say such things proves that you're just as beautiful.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.370
It is because you're so pure of thought...

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:54.170
That I must now betray you.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:56.250
Harry?

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.880
Do as you will.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.890
Lieutenant! You bastard...!

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:05.470
Forgive me!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.680
Has the Lieutenant become our enemy?

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.480
There is no other choice, but this is for the good of Queen Dianna!

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.360
I was wrong to trust you, Harry Ord.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.480
You're nothing but the Queen's lap dog!

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:19.780
So what if I am!?

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.360
Sir Guin!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:38.670
Is the Lieutenant setting out to help Dianna come aboard as well?

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.170
He has Miss Kihel with him, doesn't he?

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.260
Stay back!

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:44.760
What's the matter, Lieutenant?

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.890
Sir, the Lieutenant...

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.680
Sir Harry has taken Kihel!

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.680
Go after him!

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:50.970
Red glasses wearing jerk!

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.480
Has he betrayed us?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.060
Everyone, stop him from leaving!

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.990
The Hanger is opening.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:04.990
Is it the Militia soldiers again?

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:06.860
Please, contact and inform the White Mustache...

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.950
Lieutenant Harry has...

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.290
What's wrong?

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.450
It's the SUMO that launched.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:15.250
Mr. "Red Glasses" also went out to bring back the Queen?

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.670
No...

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:20.250
He wishes to use Kihel in her place instead!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.470
What is this!?

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.390
Dianna Counter's Mobile Suits!?

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.350
Was the intercepted transmission a trap?

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:36.270
That's not possible!

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:46.570
Is that the mustached unit the Militia soldiers excavated from the Earth?

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:51.370
It appears one of them's the infamous Devil mobile suit responsible for oppressing the space colonists.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.080
This is not a drill.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.660
I repeat, this is not a drill.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:58.670
- We'll use this formation to wipe him out!
- Yes Sir!

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.470
What should we do, Loran?

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:19.060
These mobile suits are not part of Dianna Counter.

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.690
<i>Lady Kihel is used as Lieutenant Harry's shield...</i>

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:47.610
<i>....with the intention of preventing Gym Ghingnham's ambitions.</i>

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:56.160
<i>Meanwhile, I am surprised to find myself set upon by Ghingnham's bizarre Mobile Suit forces.</i>

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:02.370
<i>Next Time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...
Battle God Ghingnham

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:05.710
"The winds of war are blowing!"

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Battle God Ghingnham</b>
